{"id":"mahabharata-3-212","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":212,"title":"द्वादशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 212 · The fire that hid in the waters","summary":{"en":"Markandeya tells of further fires, and how Agni once fled in fear and hid in the ocean, until the gods and sages found and brought him back. He ends the great lineage of fires, purified by many mantras, that carry the offerings to the gods.","kn":"ಇನ್ನಷ್ಟು ಅಗ್ನಿಗಳನ್ನೂ, ಒಮ್ಮೆ ಅಗ್ನಿ ಭಯದಿಂದ ಸಮುದ್ರದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಡಗಿದಾಗ ದೇವತೆಗಳು ಋಷಿಗಳು ಹುಡುಕಿ ಮರಳಿ ತಂದದ್ದನ್ನೂ ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅನೇಕ ಮಂತ್ರಗಳಿಂದ ಪವಿತ್ರವಾಗಿ ದೇವತೆಗಳಿಗೆ ಹವಿಸ್ಸನ್ನು ಒಯ್ಯುವ ಅಗ್ನಿಗಳ ಮಹಾವಂಶವನ್ನು ಮುಗಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"मार्कण्डेय और अग्नियों का, तथा उस घटना का वर्णन करते हैं जब अग्नि भय से भागकर समुद्र में छिप गए और देवताओं तथा ऋषियों ने उन्हें खोजकर लौटाया। वे अनेक मन्त्रों से पवित्र, देवताओं तक हवि पहुँचाने वाली अग्नियों के महान वंश का वर्णन समाप्त करते हैं।","te":"మరిన్ని అగ్నులను, ఒకప్పుడు అగ్ని భయంతో సముద్రంలో దాగగా దేవతలు, ఋషులు వెతికి తిరిగి తెచ్చిన కథను మార్కండేయుడు చెబుతాడు. అనేక మంత్రాలతో పవిత్రమై దేవతలకు హవిస్సును చేర్చే అగ్నుల మహావంశాన్ని ముగిస్తాడు.","ta":"மேலும் பல அக்னிகளையும், ஒருமுறை அக்னி அச்சத்தால் ஓடிக் கடலில் ஒளிய, தேவர்களும் முனிவர்களும் தேடி அவனைத் திரும்பக் கொணர்ந்ததையும் மார்க்கண்டேயர் சொல்கிறார். பல மந்திரங்களால் தூய்மையாகித் தேவர்களுக்கு அவியைச் சேர்க்கும் அக்னிகளின் பெருவம்சத்தை முடிக்கிறார்.","ml":"മറ്റ് അഗ്നികളെക്കുറിച്ചും, ഭയന്ന് അഗ്നി ഒരിക്കൽ സമുദ്രത്തിൽ ഒളിച്ചിരുന്നതും, ദേവന്മാരും ഋഷിമാരും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കണ്ടെത്തി തിരികെ കൊണ്ടുവന്നതും മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ പറയുന്നു. അനേകം മന്ത്രങ്ങളാൽ ശുദ്ധമാക്കപ്പെട്ട്, ദേവന്മാർക്ക് ആഹുതികൾ വഹിക്കുന്ന അഗ്നികളുടെ മഹാവംശം അദ്ദേഹം അവസാനിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.212; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आपस्य मुदिता भार्या सहस्य परमा प्रिया ।\nभूपतिर्भुवभर्ता च जनयत्पावकं परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Apa's joyful wife was the dearest of all to Saha. The lord of earth and sustainer of the world begot a supreme fire.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"भूतानां चापि सर्वेषां यं प्राहुः पावकं पतिम् ।\nआत्मा भुवनभर्तेति सान्वयेषु द्विजातिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That fire, whom they call the lord of all beings, the self and sustainer of the world, is so named among the twice-born of lineage.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"महतां चैव भूतानां सर्वेषामिह यः पतिः ।\nभगवान्स महातेजा नित्यं चरति पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The blessed, mighty-radiant fire who is lord of all great beings here ever moves about.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"अग्निर्गृहपतिर्नाम नित्यं यज्ञेषु पूज्यते ।\nहुतं वहति यो हव्यमस्य लोकस्य पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fire called Grihapati is always worshipped at sacrifices; he is the purifier who carries the offering of this world.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अपां गर्भो महाभागः सहपुत्रो महाद्भुतः ।\nभूपतिर्भुवभर्ता च महतः पतिरुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The greatly fortunate, wondrous child of the waters, with his sons, lord of earth and sustainer of the world, is called the lord of the great.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"दहन्मृतानि भूतानि तस्याग्निर्भरतोऽभवत् ।\nअग्निष्टोमे च नियतः क्रतुश्रेष्ठो भरस्य तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Burning dead creatures, he became Bharata, the fire; and at the Agnishtoma the best sacrifice is set for Bhara.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"आयान्तं नियतं दृष्ट्वा प्रविवेशार्णवं भयात् ।\nदेवास्तं नाधिगच्छन्ति मार्गमाणा यथादिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing the disciplined one coming, he entered the ocean in fear. The gods, searching in each direction, could not find him.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"दृष्ट्वा त्वग्निरथर्वाणं ततो वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nदेवानां वह हव्यं त्वमहं वीर सुदुर्बलः ।\nअथर्वन्गच्छ मध्वक्षं प्रियमेतत्कुरुष्व मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the fire saw Atharvan and said: 'You carry the offerings for the gods; I am very weak. Atharvan, go, honey-eyed one, and do this favor for me.'\""}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रेष्य चाग्निरथर्वाणमन्यं देशं ततोऽगमत् ।\nमत्स्यास्तस्य समाचख्युः क्रुद्धस्तानग्निरब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sending Atharvan, the fire went to another place. The fishes revealed him, and the angry fire spoke to them.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"भक्ष्या वै विविधैर्भावैर्भविष्यथ शरीरिणाम् ।\nअथर्वाणं तथा चापि हव्यवाहोऽब्रवीद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You will be food for living beings in many ways.' Then the offering-bearer also said words to Atharvan.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अनुनीयमानोऽपि भृशं देववाक्याद्धि तेन सः ।\nनैच्छद्वोढुं हविः सर्वं शरीरं च समत्यजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though urged strongly, in accord with the gods' word, he was unwilling to carry all the offerings, and abandoned his body.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"स तच्छरीरं संत्यज्य प्रविवेश धरां तदा ।\nभूमिं स्पृष्ट्वासृजद्धातून्पृथक्पृथगतीव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Leaving that body, he entered the earth; touching the ground, he made many different minerals.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"आस्यात्सुगन्धि तेजश्च अस्थिभ्यो देवदारु च ।\nश्लेष्मणः स्फटिकं तस्य पित्तान्मरकतं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From his mouth came fragrance and brilliance; from his bones, deodar; from his phlegm, crystal; and from his bile, emerald.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"यकृत्कृष्णायसं तस्य त्रिभिरेव बभुः प्रजाः ।\nनखास्तस्याभ्रपटलं शिराजालानि विद्रुमम् ।\nशरीराद्विविधाश्चान्ये धातवोऽस्याभवन्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From his liver came black iron, and by these three the people shone. His nails became mica, his network of veins coral; and from his body, king, came many other minerals.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"एवं त्यक्त्वा शरीरं तु परमे तपसि स्थितः ।\nभृग्वङ्गिरादिभिर्भूयस्तपसोत्थापितस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having left his body, he stayed in supreme austerity. Then Bhrigu, Angiras and others raised him up again by their austerity.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"भृशं जज्वाल तेजस्वी तपसाप्यायितः शिखी ।\nदृष्ट्वा ऋषीन्भयाच्चापि प्रविवेश महार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The fiery one blazed greatly, fed by austerity; but seeing the sages, he entered the great ocean again out of fear.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्मिन्नष्टे जगद्भीतमथर्वाणमथाश्रितम् ।\nअर्चयामासुरेवैनमथर्वाणं सुरर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When he was lost, the world was afraid and sought Atharvan, and the divine sages honored Atharvan.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"अथर्वा त्वसृजल्लोकानात्मनालोक्य पावकम् ।\nमिषतां सर्वभूतानामुन्ममाथ महार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Atharvan created the worlds, saw the fire himself, and before the eyes of all beings stirred up the great ocean.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमग्निर्भगवता नष्टः पूर्वमथर्वणा ।\nआहूतः सर्वभूतानां हव्यं वहति सर्वदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Thus the fire was lost to the blessed Atharvan before; summoned, he has carried offerings for all beings ever since.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"एवं त्वजनयद्धिष्ण्यान्वेदोक्तान्विबुधान्बहून् ।\nविचरन्विविधान्देशान्भ्रममाणस्तु तत्र वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So he produced many divine altars named in the Veda, wandering about in various regions and roaming there.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"सिन्धुवर्जं पञ्च नद्यो देविकाथ सरस्वती ।\nगङ्गा च शतकुम्भा च शरयूर्गण्डसाह्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Sindhu aside, five rivers, the Devika, the Sarasvati, the Ganga, the Shatakumbha, the Sarayu, the Gandaki...\""}},{"n":22,"text":"चर्मण्वती मही चैव मेध्या मेधातिथिस्तथा ।\nताम्रावती वेत्रवती नद्यस्तिस्रोऽथ कौशिकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"the Charmanvati, the Mahi, Medhya, Medhatithi, Tamravati, Vetravati, and three rivers, and the Kaushiki...\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तमसा नर्मदा चैव नदी गोदावरी तथा ।\nवेण्णा प्रवेणी भीमा च मेद्रथा चैव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"the Tamasa, the Narmada, the Godavari, Venna, Pravenni, Bhima and Medratha, descendant of Bharata...\""}},{"n":24,"text":"भारती सुप्रयोगा च कावेरी मुर्मुरा तथा ।\nकृष्णा च कृष्णवेण्णा च कपिला शोण एव च ।\nएता नद्यस्तु धिष्ण्यानां मातरो याः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"the Bharati, Suprayoga, the Kaveri, Murmura, the Krishna, the Krishnavenna, the Kapila and the Sona: these rivers are declared the mothers of the altars.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"अद्भुतस्य प्रिया भार्या तस्याः पुत्रो विडूरथः ।\nयावन्तः पावकाः प्रोक्ताः सोमास्तावन्त एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The wondrous one had a dear wife, and her son was Vidura-ratha. As many fires as were named, so many Somas there were as well.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अत्रेश्चाप्यन्वये जाता ब्रह्मणो मानसाः प्रजाः ।\nअत्रिः पुत्रान्स्रष्टुकामस्तानेवात्मन्यधारयत् ।\nतस्य तद्ब्रह्मणः कायान्निर्हरन्ति हुताशनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In Atri's line were born Brahma's mind-born progeny. Atri, wishing to create sons, held them within himself, and the fires draw them out of that brahmin's body.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"एवमेते महात्मानः कीर्तितास्तेऽग्नयो मया ।\nअप्रमेया यथोत्पन्नाः श्रीमन्तस्तिमिरापहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In this way I have told you of these great fires, immeasurable, glorious dispellers of darkness, and how they arose.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"अद्भुतस्य तु माहात्म्यं यथा वेदेषु कीर्तितम् ।\nतादृशं विद्धि सर्वेषामेको ह्येष हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Know that the greatness of the wondrous one is as the Vedas proclaim; for all of them this fire is one.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एक एवैष भगवान्विज्ञेयः प्रथमोऽङ्गिराः ।\nबहुधा निःसृतः कायाज्ज्योतिष्टोमः क्रतुर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This blessed one is to be known as one only, Angiras the first, who came forth in many forms from his body, as the Jyotishtoma sacrifice does.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"इत्येष वंशः सुमहानग्नीनां कीर्तितो मया ।\nपावितो विविधैर्मन्त्रैर्हव्यं वहति देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Thus I have told you this very great lineage of fires. Purified by various mantras, he carries the offerings of living beings.\""}}]}]}